# exp60 artifact hygiene — keep the curated top-level control aggregate trackable,
# ignore build outputs and raw run/log artifacts. exp60 reuses the exp58 binary by
# explicit path and builds NOTHING of its own.

# python / build scratch
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.so
*.o
*.dylib
build/

# raw per-run scratch (per-island bootstrap dirs, spike artifacts, stdio)
_control_runs/

# raw logs / HPX parcel logs
*.log
hpx.parcel.*.log
logs/

# raw run index stays ignored
control_index.jsonl

# Aggregate-write policy (see safe_write_top_aggregate in run_exp60_control.py):
#   TRACKABLE curated PASS aggregate (written only by a cluster pass):
#     - hpx_same_node_control_aggregate.json
#   IGNORED non-curated aggregates (skip/fail + redirected run-id siblings). The
#   writer emits "<base>_skip.json", "<base>_fail.json", and
#   "<base>_redirected_<stamp>_<pid>.json", so the tag follows "aggregate_"
#   directly (no extra segment) -- these patterns must NOT use "aggregate_*_skip"
#   etc., which would fail to match and let the sibling become trackable.
hpx_same_node_control_aggregate_skip.json
hpx_same_node_control_aggregate_fail.json
hpx_same_node_control_aggregate_local_skip.json
hpx_same_node_control_aggregate_redirected_*.json
